WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.122
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:05.938
Junior Makers, video 4.

3
00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:09.490
LEDs: light with a direction.

4
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.817
An LED lights when current flows the correct way.

5
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:16.280
Polarity matters.

6
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.980
Many LED kits use the longer leg for the positive side.

7
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.042
If it is the wrong way around, it stays dark — that

8
00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.590
is a useful clue when debugging.

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.207
A resistor limits current so the LED does not burn out.

10
00:00:34.257 --> 00:00:38.200
Your teacher’s kit diagram will show where it goes.

11
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.141
Let us recap.

12
00:00:41.191 --> 00:00:44.924
LEDs turn electricity into light.

13
00:00:44.974 --> 00:00:48.594
Direction, or polarity, matters.

14
00:00:48.644 --> 00:00:53.180
Next: Switches: open and close the path.
